
# Pandas Data Cleaning & Data Manipulation

## About the Project

This project is a beginner-friendly introduction to data cleaning
and manipulation using Python and Pandas.

I created a sample student dataset containing missing marks and
attendance values. I then cleaned the data, replaced values,
filtered records, sorted students, and calculated department-wise
statistics.

## Features

- Detect missing values.
- Fill missing values using column averages.
- Remove incomplete rows.
- Replace existing values.
- Filter rows based on conditions.
- Select specific columns.
- Sort students by marks.
- Group students by department.
- Calculate average marks and attendance.
- Export cleaned data to a CSV file.

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas

## Installation

Install Pandas:

```bash
pip install pandas
```

## How to Run

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/pandas-data-cleaning.git
```

Open the project folder:

```bash
cd pandas-data-cleaning
```

Run the program:

```bash
python data_cleaning.py
```

## Functions Practiced

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `df.isnull()` | Detect missing data |
| `df.fillna()` | Fill missing values |
| `df.dropna()` | Remove incomplete records |
| `df.replace()` | Replace existing values |
| `df.sort_values()` | Sort records |
| `df.groupby()` | Group and summarize data |

